      "hints": [
        "For a parametric curve, use $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}$.",
        "Differentiate $x=\\sqrt t+3$ and $y=\\ln t$ separately with respect to $t$.",
        "Divide $1/t$ by $\\tfrac12t^{-1/2}$ and simplify the power of $t$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $x = \\sqrt{t} + 3 = t^{1/2} + 3$ with respect to $t$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{1}{2}t^{-1/2} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}$$",
        "Differentiate $y = \\ln t$ with respect to $t$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{1}{t}$$",
        "Apply the parametric chain rule $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y/\\mathrm{d}t}{\\mathrm{d}x/\\mathrm{d}t}$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\frac{1}{t}}{\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{t}}{t} = \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Differentiating Parametric Curves": "Identifies the derivative of $x$ or $y$ with respect to $t$; Derives $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac2{\\sqrt t}$; Concludes with $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt t}$."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
